:"மதி","gloss":"imperative suffix"}],"gloss":"please grant"},{"surface":"பரிசில்","parts":[{"text":"பரிசில்","lemma":"பரிசில்","gloss":"gift"}],"gloss":"gift"},{"surface":"வென்வேல்","parts":[{"text":"வென்வேல்","lemma":"வென்வேல்","gloss":"victorious spear"}],"gloss":"victorious spear"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"இளம்பல்","parts":[{"text":"இளம்பல்","lemma":"இளம்பல்","gloss":"young and many"}],"gloss":"young and many"},{"surface":"கோசர்","parts":[{"text":"கோசர்","lemma":"கோசர்","gloss":"Kosar warriors"}],"gloss":"Kosar warriors"},{"surface":"விளங்குபடை","parts":[{"text":"விளங்குபடை","lemma":"விளங்குபடை","gloss":"shining weapons"}],"gloss":"shining weapons"},{"surface":"கன்மார்","parts":[{"text":"கன்மார்","lemma":"கல்","gloss":"to learn"}],"gloss":"to learn"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"இகலினர்","parts":[{"text":"இகலினர்","lemma":"இகலினர்","gloss":"those who fought"}],"gloss":"those who fought"},{"surface":"எறிந்த","parts":[{"text":"எறிந்த","lemma":"எறி","gloss":"struck"}],"gloss":"struck"},{"surface":"அகல்இலை","parts":[{"text":"அகல்","lemma":"அகல்","gloss":"wide"},{"text":"இலை","lemma":"இலை","gloss":"leaf"}],"gloss":"broad-leaved"},{"surface":"முருக்கின்","parts":[{"text":"முருக்கு","lemma":"முருக்கு","gloss":"murukku tree"},{"text":"இன்","lemma":"இன்","gloss":"oblique"}],"gloss":"of the murukku tree"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"பெருமர","parts":[{"text":"பெருமர","lemma":"பெருமரம்","gloss":"big tree (oblique)"}],"gloss":"big tree"},{"surface":"கம்பம்","parts":[{"text":"கம்பம்","lemma":"கம்பம்","gloss":"pillar"}],"gloss":"pillar"},{"surface":"போல","parts":[{"text":"போல","lemma":"போல","gloss":"like"}],"gloss":"like"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"பொருநர்க்கு","parts":[{"text":"பொருநர்","lemma":"பொருநர்","gloss":"fighters"},{"text":"க்கு","lemma":"க்கு","gloss":"dative case marker"}],"gloss":"to the enemies"},{"surface":"உலையாநின்","parts":[{"text":"உலையா","lemma":"உலை","gloss":"unyielding"},{"text":"நின்","lemma":"நின்","gloss":"your"}],"gloss":"your unyielding"},{"surface":"வலன்","parts":[{"text":"வலன்","lemma":"வலன்","gloss":"strength"}],"gloss":"strength"},{"surface":"வாழியவே","parts":[{"text":"வாழிய","lemma":"வாழி","gloss":"may you live long"},{"text":"ஏ","lemma":"ஏ","gloss":"emphasis"}],"gloss":"may you live long indeed"}]}],"literal":"See also the praise of the king's victory / When your army goes, their army / \"Do not stand before the striking army,\" they say / When their army comes, your army's / rear guard is supported, like a wide river's / dam blocked by a hill, you stood, they say / It is rare indeed, O Lord, to get your audience always / Great indeed is the suffering of my family / Right now, please grant the gift, O victorious spear! / Like the young, many Kosar warriors, to practice with shining weapons, / fought and struck the broad-leaved murukku / tree's big wooden pillar, / may your strength, unyielding to enemies, live long!","translation":"Behold the praise of the king's victory! When your army advances, the enemies say, 'Do not stand before his striking forces!' When their army attacks, you stand firm like a hill blocking a wide river, supporting your army's rear guard. O Lord, it is always rare to obtain an audience with you, while the suffering of my family is immense. Therefore, grant me your gifts right now! Like the large wooden pillar made of the broad-leaved murukku tree, which the young Kosar warriors struck with their shining weapons to practice their skills, may your strength remain unshaken by enemies. May you live long!","modern":"அரசனின் வெற்றிச் சிறப்பைப் போற்றியதையும் காண்க. உன்னுடைய படை முன்னேறிச் செல்லும்போது, பகைவர்கள் 'இவரது தாக்கும் படைக்கு முன்னால் நிற்க வேண்டாம்' என்று அஞ்சி ஓடுவர். பகைவர் படை உன்னை நோக்கி வரும்போது, அகன்ற ஆற்றைத் தடுக்கும் மலை போன்ற அணையாக நின்று உனது படையின் பின் அணியைக் காப்பாய். பெருமானே, உன்னைக் காண்பதற்கான வாய்ப்பு எப்போதும் அரிதாகவே உள்ளது. ஆனால் என் சுற்றத்தாரின் வறுமைத் துன்பமோ மிகப் பெரிதாக இருக்கிறது. வெற்றி தரும் வேலை ஏந்தியவனே, இப்போதே எனக்குப் பரிசில்களைத் தந்து அனுப்புவாயாக. இளமையான பல கோசர் குல வீரர்கள், தங்களுடைய விளங்கும் ஆயுதங்களைப் பாய்ச்சிப் பழகுவதற்காக, பகைமையோடு வெட்டிய அகன்ற இலைகளைக் கொண்ட முருக்கு மரத்தின் பெரிய தூணைப் போல, உன்னை எதிர்க்கும் பகைவர்களால் அசைக்க முடியாத உனது வலிமை என்றும் வாழ்க!","explanation":"The poet Kāviripūmpaṭṭiṉattu Kārikkaṇṇaṉār addresses the chieftain Piṭṭaṅkoṟṟaṉ, praising his military valor and requesting immediate gifts. The poet describes how the chieftain's army terrifies enemies when advancing, and how he stands like a mountain dam protecting his rear guard when attacked. He mentions that obtaining an audience with the busy chieftain is rare, while his own family's poverty is severe. To illustrate the chieftain's unyielding strength, the poet uses a vivid simile of a practice pillar made of a murukku tree, which young Kosar warriors repeatedly strike to hone their weapon skills. Just as that sturdy wooden pillar remains unshaken despite being struck, the chieftain remains victorious and unshaken by his enemies.","model":"gemini-3.5-flash"}}